  "$comment": "FROZEN snapshot (F-W19-CI-001 / dispatch C8, finding 21) of every F-id the live heuristic (suggest-pins.mjs's hasLegacyStructuralHit) classified as grandfathered at commit 132dc18 (wave-18 cutover, 2026-07-16 -- the commit that landed the declared-@pins-tag rewrite; see docs/pin-matcher-rewrite.dispatch.md). This is a CLOSED, FINITE set that only ever drains -- never grows: check-finding-regression-pins.mjs checks an id against this frozen list by MEMBERSHIP ONLY, never by re-running the retired text heuristic live. An id minted after this freeze, however legacy-shaped its decoy text, is NOT a member and therefore cannot be grandfathered -- it must earn a declared @pins tag, an allowlist entry, or it blocks the gate as an orphan (this is the exact vintage-boundary fix F-W19-CI-001 exists to add; see that finding for the pre-fix exploit). SCHEMA: every entry requires { owner, revalidate_by } (C8 discipline, matching regression-pin-allowlist.json) -- loadGrandfatherManifest throws on any malformed or incomplete entry. 'owner' is uniformly 'coordinator' because freezing this list was a coordinator-level architectural decision (the vintage boundary itself), not a per-id domain judgment call -- unlike the allowlist, where each entry's disposition is a distinct human call. MIGRATION: an id leaves this bucket (in the gate's live-run reporting, not by editing this file) the moment a real declared @pins tag lands for it, or an allowlist entry is added, or its source pin is removed -- the gate reports the shrinking count on every run (C6). DO NOT ADD new ids to this file -- that would defeat the freeze; a new orphan's fix is a declared tag, never a manifest edit. DO NOT delete an id from this file to force it clean -- the id must actually be migrated (declared tag or allowlist entry) first; deleting the manifest entry for a still-undeclared id would silently reopen it as an orphan and break the build, which is fail-closed and therefore safe, but is not migration.",
